    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "A spacious bungalow residence set on an impressive c. 0.76-acre site, ideally located just minutes from Charlestown town and less than 10 minutes from Ireland West Airport Knock.\n\nThis attractive property offers generous living accommodation, excellent outdoor space and a convenient location, making it an ideal family home or country residence.\n\nSituated approximately 3 minutes' drive from Charlestown, the property is close to a wide range of local amenities and services, including shops, primary and secondary schools, pre-school and creche facilities, church, sporting amenities and a selection of restaurants and cafés.\n\nFor commuters and travellers, Ireland West Airport Knock is less than a 10-minute drive away, while daily bus services provide connections to Galway, Sligo, Dublin and Castlebar.\nAccommodation\nThe property comprises:\n•Entrance Hall Welcoming entrance with a combination of tiled and carpeted flooring.\n•Sitting Room Bright and comfortable reception room with feature fireplace.\n•Fitted Kitchen Well-appointed kitchen with laminate flooring and oil stove.\n•Living/Dining Room Generous open living and dining space, ideal for family living and entertaining.\n•Four Bedrooms Four bright and spacious bedrooms providing excellent family accommodation.\n•Main Bathroom\n•WC\n•WC with Shower\n•Boiler House Accessed externally.\n\nOutside\nThe residence stands on a substantial c. 0.76-acre site, offering excellent space and potential for gardens, recreation and outdoor living.\nThe property also benefits from:\n•Double garage\n•Tarmacadam driveway\n•Generous grounds\n•Excellent parking provision\nFeatures\n•Spacious 4-bedroom bungalow\n•c. 0.76-acre site\n•Oil-fired central heating\n•PVC double-glazed windows\n•Double garage\n•Tarmacadam driveway\n•Convenient access to Charlestown amenities\n•Less than 10 minutes to Ireland West Airport Knock\n•Daily bus services to Galway, Sligo, Dublin and Castlebar\n"
      },
